      "text": "`format.ts` now implements the full printf-style `format(fmt, ...args)`:\n\n- **Integers** (`d i x X o`): BigInt-based, with flags, width, precision, `#` prefix/octal-leading-zero rules.\n- **Floats** (`e E f F g G`): uses exact IEEE-754 bit decomposition (`decompose`) to get the value as an exact `numerator / 10^k` fraction, then rounds with true round-half-to-even on that exact value (`roundDiv`), matching the README's rounding spec (verified against `2.675 → 2.67`, `0.5/1.5/2.5 → 0/2/2`, etc.).\n- **`g`/`G`** picks fixed vs. exponential per the exponent computed from an `e`-style rounding pass, then trims trailing zeros unless `#`.\n- **`s`/`c`** and `%%` handled directly.\n\nValidated with a differential test harness against the system `printf` across 616 float cases and 159 integer/string cases — all matched except `-0`, where the shell builtin loses the sign bit while the README explicitly requires `-0` to print as `-0.000000` (i.e., my behavior is correct there, not the test).",
